  "body": "\nTwo workflows writing ADRs into one repository could reserve the same number because `number_guards.py` read only its own flat task files. Fetch and read every `origin/spacedock-state/*` branch, include folder-form tasks, and refuse an added ADR number held by another task before the merge ask (R8). Exclude the checked task's pushed copy only on its own state branch when its state checkout has `origin`; leave base-number collisions to R5.\n\nWarn when a state checkout has no `origin` or a fetch falls back to local refs. Amend ADR 0002 with the Captain-approved shared-state obligation. The workflow template changes only its stale help-rule list and collision parenthesis, reducing its word budget by six. No version or CI configuration changes.\n\nValidation:\n- `python3 -B kc-dev-flow-2/scripts/test_number_guards.py`: 37 tests passed, including local-origin single-branch and folder-task replays.\n- Eleven behavioral/help mutations caught; unchanged base fails seven of the nine cross-workflow cases. Budget-step removal, a wrong Captain quote and an invalid ADR status are also refused.\n- Existing task parsing matches on 142 committed live/archive tasks. Independent recount: startup 5993 to 5987 normalized words; lint budget 5939 to 5933 whitespace words; no clean lifecycle moment increases.\n- Repository `lint-skills.py`, installed ADR lint, installed and candidate number checks, design checks and comment ratio passed. Added comments: 0.5%, maximum 5%.\n- With FO approval, the existing dispatch replay now checks both exact AC-6 diagnostic lines instead of empty stderr. Only that assertion changes in the additional test file; targeted replay passes. Reruns at `6a0a4aec60bb5900a0d363bae912acc5714f5974`: dispatch test file 115 run, one optional-input skip, exit 0; full package suite 965 run, seven optional-input skips, exit 0. Supplemental extension suites and local Spacedock dispatch contracts pass, with four optional release-integration skips.\n\nShared reads leave a race between reservation and state push; this does not add an atomic lock. Workflows without a pushed state branch remain invisible, and a failed fetch can read stale refs with a warning. Local transport checks do not prove native worker execution or GitHub CI.\n\nPublication is handed to FO: the product branch is committed locally, not pushed; no PR has been opened. FO opens the Draft PR, runs RoboRev and reads CI on the PR head. CI cost per PR was not measured.\n\nRoboRev: run by FO: `clean on 6a0a4aec6; evidence=roborev:1577`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
